    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Forme",
     "md": "**am / is / are + going to + verbe** : I **am going to** study. · She **is going to** visit her aunt. · They **are going to** play.\nNégation : She **isn't going to** come. Question : **Are** you **going to** travel ? — Yes, I am. / No, I'm not."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Deux emplois",
     "md": "1. Un **projet décidé** à l'avance : I'm going to visit Kribi in August.\n2. Une **prévision avec une preuve** : Look at the clouds ! It's going to rain.\nIndicateurs : tomorrow, next week, next year, tonight, in two days."
    },
